<article class="env-proposition" id="0922">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0922">Proposition <span data-tag="0922">15.96.2</span>.</a> Let $A$ be a Noetherian ring. Let $I \subset A$ be an ideal. The functor which sends $K \in D(A)$ to the derived limit $K' = R\mathop{\mathrm{lim}}\nolimits ( K \otimes _ A^\mathbf {L} A/I^ n )$ is the left adjoint to the inclusion functor $D_{comp}(A) \to D(A)$ constructed in Lemma <a href="/tag/091V" data-tag="091V">15.93.10</a>. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Say $(f_1, \ldots , f_ r) = I$ and let $K_ n^\bullet $ be the Koszul complex with respect to $f_1^ n, \ldots , f_ r^ n$. By Lemma <a href="/tag/0920" data-tag="0920">15.93.18</a> it suffices to prove that 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  R\mathop{\mathrm{lim}}\nolimits (K \otimes _ A^\mathbf {L} K_ n^\bullet ) = R\mathop{\mathrm{lim}}\nolimits (K \otimes _ A^\mathbf {L} A/(f_1^ n, \ldots , f_ r^ n) ) = R\mathop{\mathrm{lim}}\nolimits (K \otimes _ A^\mathbf {L} A/I^ n ).  \]
</div>
    <p>
       By Lemma <a href="/tag/0921" data-tag="0921">15.96.1</a> the pro-objects $\{ K_ n^\bullet \} $ and $\{ A/(f_1^ n, \ldots , f_ r^ n)\} $ of $D(A)$ are isomorphic. It is clear that the pro-objects $\{ A/(f_1^ n, \ldots , f_ r^ n)\} $ and $\{ A/I^ n\} $ are isomorphic. Thus the map from left to right is an isomorphism by Lemma <a href="/tag/091L" data-tag="091L">15.89.12</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>